<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Revolt of the Comuneros (Paraguay)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1721">1721</a>–<a href="/years/1735">1735</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Revolt of the Comuneros was a rising of Spanish settlers in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a> between 1721 and 1735 against the authority of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missions' control of Guaraní labour. Led at first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-antequera-y-castro">José de Antequera</a>, who was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in 1731, it was finally crushed by the governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruno-mauricio-de-zabala">Bruno Mauricio de Zabala</a>, in 1735.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-comuneros-paraguay.jpg" alt="Revolt of the Comuneros (Paraguay)" width="300" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SnowFire Using as a base: Camilo Sanchez · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Viceroyalty_Peru_1721_comuneros.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
